  "id": "Compound::DB00035 - Gene::554",
  "verbalization": "Desmopressin, through its resemblance to Linaclotide and Felypressin, shares a common ancestry with Terlipressin, which binds to Avpr2. This suggests a potential mechanism where desmopressin, as a therapeutic hormone analogue, may interact with Avpr2 via a shared structural or functional relationship. The evidence points to a pathway where desmopressin, as part of a heterodetic cyclic peptide family, may exert its effects by binding to Avpr2, possibly through a mechanism involving antidiuretic hormone-like activity. The recurring theme of resemblance and common ancestry supports a hypothesis that desmopressin's interaction with Avpr2 is mediated by its structural similarity to other antidiuretic hormone analogues, which in turn bind to the same receptor. This connection is further supported by the shared classification of desmopressin and its analogs as therapeutic hormones, reinforcing the likelihood of a functional relationship between desmopressin and Avpr2.",
